      "kind": "hypothesis",
      "title": "Investigation assessment",
      "detail": "Checkout service is returning HTTP 503 with no origin telemetry. Current policies block all recovery actions due to missing diagnostic evidence. The dependency topology shows that checkout depends on payments and inventory, which in turn depend on ledger and notifications. However, no logs, traces, or deployment history are available to identify the root cause. Historical incident memory indicates a prior resolution via disabling a payments feature flag, but this outcome is not applicable under current constraints due to absence of current diagnostic data. Without origin logs and request traces, no action\u2014rollback, feature flag disable, or restart\u2014is justified by current evidence. The policy block is explicitly tied to the absence of origin diagnostics, as defined in the telemetry-gap policy.",
